---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailPortfolio = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=UGC%20portfolio%20review%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20content";
const emailGeneral = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=UGC%20portfolio%20%E2%80%94%20general%20inquiry";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="UGC Portfolio Examples: What Great Portfolios Look Like | OKAD"
  description="See what separates good UGC portfolios from great ones. Real analysis of portfolio structure, essential elements, common mistakes, and niche-specific tips from an agency that works with 700+ creators."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          UGC Portfolio Examples: <span class="text-accent">What Great Portfolios Actually Look Like</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Your portfolio is the single most important asset in your UGC career. We have reviewed 2,000+ creator portfolios. This guide breaks down what separates the portfolios that land deals from the ones that collect dust.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailPortfolio} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Get portfolio feedback &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>700+ creators</span>
          <span>2,000+ reviews</span>
          <span>5&ndash;8 videos</span>
          <span>Niche-specific</span>
          <span>Portfolio &rarr; deals</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">Why Your Portfolio Matters</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F3AF;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">73% of Deals Start Here</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">In our creator network, nearly three out of four brand deals begin with a portfolio review. The portfolio is the decision-making moment.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F3AC;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">5&ndash;8 Videos Are Enough</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">The best-performing portfolios contain between five and eight videos. This range gives brands enough to assess your range while ensuring every piece is strong.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4B0;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">2x Response Rate Increase</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Creators who switched from a Google Drive link to a proper portfolio page saw their brand response rate roughly double.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "Six Essential Elements", href: "#elements" },
            { num: "03", text: "The Ideal Portfolio Structure", href: "#structure" },
            { num: "04", text: "Common Mistakes", href: "#mistakes" },
            { num: "05", text: "Niche-Specific Tips", href: "#niches" },
            { num: "06", text: "What We Look For", href: "#analysis" },
            { num: "07", text: "Good vs Great Portfolio", href: "#comparison" },
            { num: "08", text: "Portfolio Checklist", href: "#checklist" },
            { num: "09", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Your portfolio is your sales team</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A brand manager spends 12 seconds on a portfolio before deciding to scroll deeper or move on</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Your portfolio must answer three questions: can they create content that fits, have they done this before, and how do I hire them</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A dedicated web-based portfolio doubles brand response rate vs Google Drive links</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">At OKAD, we work with over 700 UGC creators across beauty, tech, food, fitness, and lifestyle. We see every format imaginable: Canva decks, Google Drive folders, Notion pages, Instagram highlights, and dedicated portfolio sites. After years of matching creators to brand campaigns, we know exactly which portfolios get opened, which get bookmarked, and which get ignored.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A brand manager evaluating UGC creators spends an average of 12 seconds on a portfolio before deciding to scroll deeper or move on. In those 12 seconds, your portfolio needs to answer three questions: Can this person create content that fits our brand? Have they done this before? How do I hire them?</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Creators in our network who switched from a Google Drive link to a proper portfolio page saw their brand response rate roughly double. A dedicated, well-structured portfolio page signals professionalism before anyone watches a single frame of your content.</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Deals start:</strong> 73% begin with a portfolio review</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Sweet spot:</strong> 5&ndash;8 videos per portfolio</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Response rate:</strong> 2x increase with a dedicated web page</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Network:</strong> 700+ creators reviewed regularly</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 Essential Elements -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="elements">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Essential Elements</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Six elements every UGC portfolio needs</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A clear opening statement that tells brands your niche and outcome in one sentence</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Video work front and center &mdash; playable, not thumbnails or screenshots</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand logos, rates, social proof, and a single clear CTA</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">After reviewing thousands of creator portfolios across our network, these are the six non-negotiable elements that appear in every portfolio that consistently wins brand deals.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">01. A clear opening statement</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The first line of your portfolio should tell a brand exactly what you do and who you do it for. Not your life story. Not a list of platforms. One sentence: niche, content type, and the outcome you deliver.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>State your niche and content type upfront</li>
          <li>Mention the outcome brands care about</li>
          <li>Skip the generic "passionate creator" intro</li>
          <li>Keep it under 20 words</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">02. Video work front and center</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Your best three to five videos should be the first thing a brand sees after your intro. Not thumbnails. Not screenshots. Playable videos with native sound. If a brand manager has to click through to another site or request file access, you have already lost them.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>Lead with your strongest piece, not your newest</li>
          <li>Include a mix of content types (testimonial, unboxing, tutorial)</li>
          <li>Make sure every video loads and plays instantly</li>
          <li>Remove anything older than 12 months unless it went viral</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">03. Brand logos and collaboration history</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Even if you have worked with two brands, show them. Logos create instant credibility. A portfolio without brand names feels like a resume without job titles. Group them visually so a scanning eye catches them in under two seconds.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>Use recognizable logos, not just text names</li>
          <li>Group by industry if you have 5+ brands</li>
          <li>Include spec work clearly labeled as such</li>
          <li>Update after every new collaboration</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">04. Rates and availability</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Brands do not want to play email ping-pong to find out your pricing. Include at least a starting rate or a range. Creators who show rates get 40% more inbound inquiries in our experience, because brand managers can immediately see whether the budget fits.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>Show starting rates, not exact quotes</li>
          <li>List turnaround time for standard deliverables</li>
          <li>Mention if you offer usage rights separately</li>
          <li>Include your preferred contact method</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">05. Social proof and metrics</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">If your video hit 500K views, say so. If a brand's CPA dropped 30% after running your creative, include that number. Social proof converts hesitant brand managers into paying clients faster than any bio ever will.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>Include view counts on standout videos</li>
          <li>Show performance metrics where available</li>
          <li>Add client testimonials even if they are short</li>
          <li>Link to live posts so brands can verify</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">06. A single clear CTA</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Every portfolio needs exactly one call to action. Not three. Not a paragraph of options. One button or one email address. The easier you make it to reach you, the more brands will actually do it.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li>Use a specific email, not a contact form</li>
          <li>Add a booking link for quick calls</li>
          <li>Place the CTA after your video section</li>
          <li>Repeat it at the bottom of the page</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 Portfolio Structure -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="structure">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; Structure</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The ideal portfolio structure, top to bottom</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Think of your portfolio as a funnel &mdash; each section pulls the brand manager deeper</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Hero, featured reel, brand logos, video grid, about/rates, contact CTA</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Make the next action obvious at every step</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Think of your portfolio as a funnel. Each section should pull the brand manager deeper into your work and make the next action obvious. Here is the order that works.</p>

        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Hero Section.</strong> Your name, one-line positioning, and a professional photo. This is not a headshot from your phone camera. Invest in one good photo.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Featured Reel.</strong> Your single best video, auto-playing with sound off. This is the piece that makes a brand manager stop scrolling and start watching.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Brand Logos.</strong> A clean row of logos from brands you have worked with. Even two or three logos change the perception of your portfolio entirely.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Video Grid.</strong> Your top 5 to 8 videos organized by content type or niche. Each video needs a label: brand, format, and platform.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>About and Rates.</strong> A brief bio focused on what makes you different, your starting rates, turnaround time, and the types of content you specialize in.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Contact CTA.</strong> A clear, prominent way to reach you. An email address, a booking link, or both. No contact forms that disappear into a void.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 Common Mistakes -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="mistakes">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Mistakes</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Six portfolio mistakes that cost you brand deals</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Leading with follower count instead of content quality</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Using PDFs or Google Drive folders instead of a web page</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Each mistake is fixable in under an hour</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">We see these errors in the majority of portfolios that come through our creator intake process. Each one is fixable in under an hour, and fixing them can make a dramatic difference in how brands respond to your work.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Mistake</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Why it hurts</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Leading with follower count</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brands hiring UGC creators care about content quality, not your audience size. Your follower count is irrelevant when the brand is running your video as a paid ad. Lead with your work, not your metrics.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Using a PDF or Google Drive folder</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">PDFs do not play video. Google Drive links require access requests and feel unprofessional. Both break when you update your work. A web-based portfolio stays current and loads instantly on any device.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Showing everything you have ever made</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">More is not better. A portfolio with 40 videos tells a brand you cannot curate. Show your 5 to 8 strongest pieces. Every extra video that is not excellent actively weakens the ones that are.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">No context on each video</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">A video without a label is just a clip. Add the brand name, the content type (testimonial, tutorial, unboxing), and the platform it was made for. Context turns a reel into a case study.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Outdated work from 2+ years ago</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">UGC styles change fast. Content that looked fresh in 2024 can feel dated today. If your portfolio includes work from before 2025, remove it unless it has exceptional performance metrics attached.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">No mobile optimization</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Over 70% of brand managers first open your portfolio on their phone. If your layout breaks on mobile, your text is too small to read, or your videos do not autoplay, you are losing most of your audience.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Niche-Specific Tips -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="niches">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Niches</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What winning portfolios look like in each niche</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">A beauty portfolio and a tech portfolio require fundamentally different approaches</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Tech UGC is the highest-paying niche at $500&ndash;$2,000 per video</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Niche specialists get picked over generalists</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A beauty portfolio and a tech portfolio require fundamentally different approaches. Here is what we look for in each niche when evaluating creators for brand campaigns.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Beauty and Skincare</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The strongest beauty portfolios lead with close-up application shots and before-after sequences. Lighting quality matters more here than in any other niche. Show texture, show glow, show the product in use.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Key elements:</strong> Get-ready-with-me format, close-up product shots, natural lighting, skin texture visibility</li>
          <li><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Include both "raw skin" and "finished look" videos. Brands want to see you can sell transformation, not just application.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Food and Beverage</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Food UGC portfolios need to make viewers hungry. That means overhead shots, steam, drizzles, and the satisfying first bite. Audio matters enormously in this niche: the crunch, the sizzle, the pour.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Key elements:</strong> Overhead angles, ASMR audio, recipe walkthroughs, appetizing presentation</li>
          <li><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Show at least one video with a full recipe flow and one that is purely aesthetic. Brands need both educational and aspirational content.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Tech and SaaS</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Tech UGC is the highest-paying niche, with rates reaching $500 to $2,000 per video. Your portfolio needs to demonstrate that you can explain complex products simply and make screen recordings feel dynamic.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Key elements:</strong> Screen recordings with face overlay, demo walkthroughs, problem-solution structure, clean audio</li>
          <li><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Include at least one video where you explain a technical feature to a non-technical audience. This is the skill brands pay premium rates for.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Fitness and Wellness</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Fitness portfolios succeed when they show energy and authenticity. Avoid overly polished gym footage. Brands in this space want real workouts, real sweat, and genuine reactions to products.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Key elements:</strong> Workout demonstrations, supplement unboxings, lifestyle integration, energetic delivery</li>
          <li><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Show yourself using the product in a real workout, not just holding it and talking. Action shots outsell talking heads in this niche by a wide margin.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Mid CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(22px,3.5vw,32px)] tracking-[-0.02em] text-white mb-3">Need help with your portfolio?</h2>
          <p class="text-[15px] text-muted max-w-[480px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-6">We work with 700+ UGC creators and review portfolios daily. Whether you need a full portfolio audit, niche-specific guidance, or want to join our creator network, we can help.</p>
          <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap">
            <a href={emailPortfolio} class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-white text-ink hover:bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Get portfolio feedback &rarr;</a>
            <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold text-muted border border-white/15 hover:text-white hover:border-white/30 transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
