    <!-- 06 What We Look For -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="analysis">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Analysis</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What we actually look for when reviewing portfolios</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">First impression in 0&ndash;3 seconds: clean layout and clear positioning</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Content quality in 3&ndash;15 seconds: hook, lighting, audio</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Range, consistency, and professionalism in 15&ndash;60 seconds</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">When a creator applies to join OKAD's network of 700+ creators, our team evaluates their portfolio against a specific set of criteria. Here is the internal framework we use.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">First Impression (0 to 3 seconds)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Does the portfolio look professional at a glance? We check for a clean layout, a clear name and positioning statement, and whether we can immediately tell what kind of content this person creates. Portfolios that open with a wall of text or a generic bio get closed immediately.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The strongest portfolios we see have a single sentence above the fold that tells us the creator's niche and their angle. Something specific, like "I make testimonial-style ads for DTC skincare brands" rather than "UGC creator with a passion for storytelling."</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Content Quality (3 to 15 seconds)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">We watch the first five seconds of the top video. If the hook is weak, the lighting is poor, or the audio is unclear, we have already formed an opinion. The opening clip in your portfolio carries disproportionate weight because it is the only piece most reviewers will watch in full.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">We specifically look for: natural delivery (not reading from a script with dead eyes), good lighting (natural light works perfectly), clean audio (no background noise, no echo), and a strong opening hook that would stop someone scrolling on their phone.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Range and Consistency (15 to 30 seconds)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">We scan the remaining videos to check for range. Can this creator do different formats? Testimonial and unboxing and tutorial? Or is every video the same talking-head setup? Range matters because brands need versatility within a campaign.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">At the same time, we look for consistency. Every video should feel like it was made by the same creator in terms of quality level, even if the format varies. A portfolio with one amazing video and four mediocre ones tells us the amazing one might have been a fluke.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Professionalism (30 to 60 seconds)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Finally, we check the practical details. Are rates listed? Is there a clear way to contact this person? Do they mention turnaround time? Is their bio written in clear, grammatically correct English? These details do not seem creative, but they signal whether this person will be reliable to work with on a real campaign with real deadlines.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

