        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "How many videos should a UGC portfolio include?", a: "Five to eight is the sweet spot. Enough to demonstrate range, few enough that every piece is genuinely strong. We review hundreds of creator portfolios each month at OKAD, and the ones that convert best are tightly curated rather than comprehensive." },
          { q: "Should I include spec work or only paid brand deals?", a: "Absolutely include spec work, especially if you are early in your career. Just label it honestly. A well-produced spec video for a brand you admire shows initiative and skill. What matters is the quality of the content, not whether someone paid for it." },
          { q: "Do I need a website or can I use a portfolio platform?", a: "A dedicated portfolio platform built for UGC creators is usually better than a general website builder. Platforms designed for creator portfolios handle video playback, mobile responsiveness, and quick updates far better than a Squarespace site you built yourself." },
          { q: "How often should I update my portfolio?", a: "After every significant project. At minimum, review it monthly and swap out your weakest piece for your newest strong work. A portfolio that has not been updated in six months signals to brands that you are not actively working." },
          { q: "What if I only have content for one niche?", a: "That is actually a strength, not a weakness. Brands prefer specialists. A portfolio focused entirely on beauty UGC or tech reviews tells a brand that you understand their audience deeply. Generalist portfolios get overlooked more often than niche ones." },
          { q: "Should I include pricing in my portfolio?", a: "Yes. At minimum, include a starting rate or a price range. Brands respect transparency, and it filters out inquiries that would never match your budget. Creators who display rates tend to attract more serious leads with faster turnaround on bookings." },
          { q: "How do brands actually discover UGC portfolios?", a: "Through three main channels: direct outreach from creators who include their portfolio link in pitch emails, creator directories and marketplaces, and organic search. Having a web-based portfolio that search engines can index dramatically increases your inbound opportunities." },
